<v Ira Glass>I'm just going to come in here now in 2026. This interruption is happening right now. I have to say something else that hearing this recording reminds me of, and that is that when I look at pictures of my mom, it's just-- I just feel a sense of fondness for my mom.
<v Ira Glass>我这就切回2026年说两句。这个打断现在正在发生。我必须说点别的，听到这段录音让我想起了什么，那就是当我看着我妈的照片时，我只会——我只会对妈妈感到一种深切的喜爱。

00:17:51.240 --> 00:18:19.140
<v Ira Glass>But when you hear somebody's voice, it's so much more powerful. Like, it's just like-- I feel like it's like she's alive, talking to me again. And I'm having all the feelings that I had when she was alive. Like, really, as this tape was playing, beat by beat, moment by moment, I feel like I'm experiencing this conversation the same way I did 30 years ago. Like, just-- yeah. And pictures cannot do that.
<v Ira Glass>但当你听到某人的声音时，那种冲击力要强烈得多。就好像——我觉得她就像活过来了一样，又在跟我说话。我拥有了她活着时所拥有的一切感受。真的，当这段录音播放时，伴随着每一个节拍、每一个瞬间，我觉得自己正在以30年前完全相同的方式经历这段对话。就像——是的。而照片是做不到这一点的。

