<v Ira Glass>I'm just going to stop this tape right there. I have three things to say about this tape. Number one, "formerly of Europe?" Number two, of course, no appointment is necessary. She already knows you're coming. And number three, this is my father in 1956, three years before I was born. He's 23 years old.
<v Ira Glass>我得把这段录音就在这里暂停一下。关于这段录音我有三点要说。第一，“曾经旅居欧洲？”第二，当然，无需预约。她早就知道你要来了。第三，这是1956年的我父亲，在我出生前三年。他当时23岁。

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:58.780
<v Dad>And coming up right now, news about a wonderful appliance from Norman R. Mitchell, just for the homemakers, as we said before. We're talking about an electric dryer. And my friend, if the lady in your house has her heart set on an electric dryer, here's some big news for you from Norman R. Mitchell. Right now, they are featuring the new 1957 Frigidaire Filtr-omatic Electric Dryer at an unbelievable low price.
<v Dad>接下来要播的是关于诺曼·R·米切尔的一款精彩电器的消息，专为家庭主妇准备，正如我们刚才所说。我们要说的是电动干衣机。我的朋友，如果你家里的女主人一心想要一台电动干衣机，诺曼·R·米切尔这里有好消息要告诉你。现在，他们正在以难以置信的超低价推出全新的1957年款富及第滤清自动电动干衣机。

00:23:58.780 --> 00:24:32.690
<v Ira Glass>My father started in radio when he was 19, the same age I was when I started. He began at the college station at the University of Maryland, and after graduation, got a job spinning records at a commercial station in Baltimore. Then he was drafted. And at the time of this particular recording, my father was actually in the Army, stationed in Virginia. But he wanted a career in radio so badly that every Sunday morning, at the break of dawn, he would leave his wife and his five-month-old baby, my older sister, and drive up to Baltimore to do a four-hour program.
<v Ira Glass>我父亲19岁时就开始从事广播工作，这和我开始时的年龄一样。他从马里兰大学的校园广播站起步，毕业后在巴尔的摩的一家商业电台找到了一份打碟的工作。后来他应征入伍。在录制这段特定音频的时候，我父亲其实正在弗吉尼亚州的军队服役。但他太渴望拥有广播事业了，以至于每个星期天清晨，天蒙蒙亮的时候，他就会离开妻子和五个月大的宝宝——也就是我的大姐，开车赶到巴尔的摩去做一个四小时的节目。

00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:48.690
