00:28:38.600 --> 00:29:13.540
<v Ira Glass>Not long after he got out of the Army, my dad decided that radio was no way to make a living. And after a series of jobs, he decided to become a certified public accountant. He was a typical workaholic suburban dad, off to the office at 7:00 in the morning, back at 6:30 for dinner. Exhausted after that, he would sit in his yellow recliner in front of the TV and fall asleep. He started his own business, struggled to establish it, worked lots of nights and weekends. During tax season, from January to April 15, we would barely see him.
<v Ira Glass>我爸爸退伍后不久，就认定电台根本无法谋生。在做过一系列工作之后，他决定成为一名注册会计师。他是个典型的郊区工作狂爸爸，早上7点出门去办公室，晚上6点半回家吃晚餐。在那之后他已经精疲力竭，便会坐在电视机前的黄色躺椅上睡着。他自己创业，艰难地维持着公司的发展，度过了无数个加班的夜晚和周末。在每年的报税季，也就是从1月到4月15日，我们几乎难得见到他一面。

