<v Ira Glass>In our house, when I was growing up, was an old reel-to-reel tape recorder, a little consumer unit that my mother and my sisters and I would goof around on from time to time, recorded singing or telling stories. And while my mom appears on these tapes a lot, my father does not appear on them once. He simply was not there to be recorded. The only time he's mentioned on all of these tapes is this. I'm going to play this moment to you. My mother is cooing to my older sister, Randi, who's probably-- I don't know-- a year old, a year and a half old.
<v Ira Glass>在我小时候的家里，有一台旧的盘式录音机，那是一台小型消费级设备，我和妈妈、姐姐们偶尔会在上面胡闹，录下唱歌或讲故事的声音。虽然我妈妈在这些磁带里出现了很多次，但我爸爸却一次也没有出现。他根本不在场，无法被录进去。在所有这些磁带中，唯一提到他的一次是这样的。我把这个片段放给你们听。我妈妈正在哄我大姐兰迪（Randi），她当时可能——我不知道——一岁，或者一岁半左右。

