00:30:21.030 --> 00:30:26.460
<v Ira Glass>These days, my dad explains his decision to leave radio and become an accountant this way.
<v Ira Glass>如今，我爸爸这样解释他当年放弃广播转行做会计的决定。

00:30:26.460 --> 00:30:49.280
<v Dad>By that time, I had realized that radio was not for me. And what happened would be a new program director would come in, and if you weren't the apple of that guy's eye, then you were out of a job. You gotta go start looking for a job again. Even though that never happened to me, I could see it happening to other people, and I wanted to be in control of my own destiny. And I decided that it wasn't going to work out.
<v Dad>到了那个时候，我意识到广播并不适合我。当时的情况是，会来一个新的节目总监，如果你不合那个人的眼缘，那你就会失业。你就得重新开始找工作。尽管这种事从来没有发生在我身上，但我能看到它发生在别人身上，而我想掌控自己的命运。我决定那条路行不通。

00:30:49.280 --> 00:30:49.780
<v Ira Glass>And that was--
<v Ira Glass>那是——

00:30:49.420 --> 00:30:51.020
<v Dad>For me, that was not going to work out.
<v Dad>对我来说，那条路是行不通的。

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:52.520
<v Ira Glass>And that was 1959?
<v Ira Glass>那是1959年吗？

